> Exact parity cycles are smaller objects

Taking the low bit turns addition into XOR. Normalize the ring to oldest-first
order before packing its k parities into a mask; this removes the changing
physical index from the projected state. For j2,k5 the mask update drops the
oldest bit and appends old_bit0 XOR old_bit3. A repeated normalized mask proves
a cycle of this projected deterministic recurrence, not a repeat of the
complete64-bit engine.

The native orbit inspector advances an independent complete engine copy,
captures each actual distinct normalized mask, and reports the first repeated
mask’s offset and cycle length. The original engine and cached distribution
state are untouched. It supports k<=63 and an explicit distinct-mask cap;
incomplete inspection has no inferred period.

For this tiny lag pair, find a seeded representative of every one of the32
parity masks and inspect its complete finite orbit. The zero mask has period1
and the31 nonzero masks share a period31 cycle. This exhaustive projection check
does not establish the full word period or acceptable simulation quality.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lagged_fibonacci_parity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/random/lagged_fibonacci_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <map>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::map<std::uint64_t, std::pair<std::uint64_t, std::size_t>> periods;
    for (std::uint64_t seed = 0; seed < 4096 && periods.size() < 32; ++seed) {
        dm::random::LaggedFibonacci64 g(seed, 2, 5);
        const auto o = dm::random::lagged_fibonacci_parity_orbit(g, 32);
        if (!o.complete)
            throw std::runtime_error("incomplete tiny parity orbit");
        periods.try_emplace(o.masks.front(), seed, o.period);
    }
    if (periods.size() != 32)
        throw std::runtime_error("not all parity states represented");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual initial parity mask | representative seed | actual complete parity period |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto[mask, example] : periods) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", mask, example.first, example.second);
        x.push_back(mask);
        y.push_back(example.second);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "parity period", {37, 99, 235}, 5).y_limits(-1, 38).title(
        "All32 normalized parity states for j2,k5").x_label(
        "initial oldest-first parity mask").y_label("exact observed parity period").save_svg("build/lagged_fibonacci_parity.svg");
}
```
