> Lag choices and incomplete inspection

Hold seed2026 fixed while changing lag pairs, including a reducible small
recurrence and the default j24,k55. This is a family of separate complete engine
constructions. At most4096 distinct parity states are inspected per case. A
capped incomplete result is printed as unknown period rather than treating zero
or the cap as a measured cycle length. The plot includes only completed tiny
projected cycles. It is not a benchmark or a demonstration of the default
engine’s full period.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lagged_fibonacci_lags.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/random/lagged_fibonacci_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::size_t ordinal = 0;
    std::print("| case ordinal | actual short lag | actual long lag | retained distinct parity masks | " "complete | actual parity period or unknown |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (auto[j, k] : std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t, std::size_t>>{{1, 3},
                                                                       {1, 4},
                                                                       {2, 4},
                                                                       {2, 5},
                                                                       {3, 7},
                                                                       {24, 55}}) {
        dm::random::LaggedFibonacci64 g(2026, j, k);
        const auto o = dm::random::lagged_fibonacci_parity_orbit(g, 4096);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", ordinal, j, k,
                   o.masks.size(), o.complete,
                   o.complete ? std::to_string(o.period) : "unknown");
        if (o.complete) {
            x.push_back(ordinal);
            y.push_back(o.period);
        }
        ++ ordinal;
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "complete only", {37, 99, 235}, 6).y_limits(-5, 160).title(
        "Completed parity cycles of explicit lag cases").x_label(
        "case ordinal, see computed table").y_label("exact observed parity period").save_svg("build/lagged_fibonacci_lags.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| case ordinal | actual short lag | actual long lag | retained distinct parity masks | complete | actual parity period or unknown |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |
| 0 | 1 | 3 | 7 | true | 7 |
| 1 | 1 | 4 | 15 | true | 15 |
| 2 | 2 | 4 | 6 | true | 6 |
| 3 | 2 | 5 | 31 | true | 31 |
| 4 | 3 | 7 | 127 | true | 127 |
| 5 | 24 | 55 | 4096 | false | unknown |
\image(figures/lagged_fibonacci_lags.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual parity-cycle outcomes under an explicit inspection ceiling.)
\alttext(Only completed cycle lengths appear in the plot; the default long ring’s capped result remains unknown if no repeat was observed.)

> Scope and verification

Raw observations share the canonical modular transition and do not replay
prefixes. Consuming trace admission counts both complete boundary rings plus
every transition record,2*k+count, before allocating all required storage and
before advancing the caller engine. The default million-entry ceiling excludes
fields/capacities/bytes/RAM; zero disables only this optional cap.
Allocation/quota failure leaves the caller engine unadvanced. The separate
parity-orbit bound controls retained distinct masks of an independent copy and
reports incomplete inspection honestly.

An independent exact modular SplitMix/ring model checked16 seed/lag controls
and16000 actual updates, including every original operand, slot and intended
wraparound. A separate binary shift-register model checked38 projected orbits,
including all32 states of the original tiny lag pair. Another16000 raw outputs
matched the frozen engine exactly. Native controls verify complete
pre-consumption admission, owned boundary snapshots, nonmutating orbit
inspection and inherited normal-cache behavior. Fresh companion-file and
exact11-symbol changed-engine documentation scopes passed; the broader shared
random-file backlog remains outside the completed manifest. The ten-report
shared build passed141 native CTest cases,45 directly instrumented
address/undefined-behaviour sanitizer cases,90 compiled/executed public
examples,412/412 scoped file definitions plus11/11 changed lagged-Fibonacci
engine definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. All four complete
report programs executed and all four native figures were visually reviewed.
Receipts and repeatable checks are retained under
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-184-193/`.

> References

D. E. Knuth, The Art of Computer Programming, Volume2: Seminumerical Algorithms,
third edition(1997), chapter3,
[author’s book page|https://www-cs-faculty.stanford.edu/~knuth/taocp.html]. The
native SplitMix initialization, physical-ring observations and explicitly finite
parity inspection are specified above; arbitrary-lag maximal-period claims are
not inferred.
